# The winery's hands (lane 28, 2026-10-08: "more people walking around and doing things"). While the winery is lost,
# Ionel keeps watch over the lane, Tereza keeps the camp's washing and Horia splits wood; once the family is home,
# Ovidiu dresses the vines, Andrei picks the east rows and Old Silviu is back at his casks. And the ravens, always,
# who talk under Speak with Animals. Unvoiced for now.

~ watch
Ionel: Keep your voice down. They come up the rows at dusk, the twig things, and I'd like to hear them before they hear me. If you're going up to the winery, go now, while there's light.
-> watch_menu

~ watch_menu
* What would you most like, Ionel? -> watch_want
* [if not flag.ionel_crossbow_known] [Insight DC 12] (Watch how he holds the crossbow.) -> watch_secret | watch_miss
* Good luck. -> END

~ watch_want
Ionel [weary]: Eight hours with my boots off and both eyes shut, and nobody shouting from the trees.
Ionel: I don't even want a good dream. Just the black part between lying down and getting up.
-> watch_menu

~ watch_secret
set ionel_crossbow_known
Narrator: The crossbow lies slack across his arm, and the quarrel bag at his belt holds nothing but a dry stick.
Ionel [afraid]: Don't say it loud. I dropped the quarrel bag in the brambles three nights ago when the hedge moved.
Ionel [weary]: If the twig-men come up the lane, I'll have to point it very hard and hope they're polite.
-> watch_menu

~ watch_miss
Narrator: He shifts the heavy stock under his arm so you cannot quite see the groove.
-> watch_menu

~ washer
Tereza: I came out from Vallaki to pick grapes for one season. That was four years ago. Hand me that peg. No, the other one.
-> washer_menu

~ washer_menu
* Are you going back to Vallaki? -> washer_want
* [if not flag.tereza_sweet_known] [Insight DC 12] (Watch how she talks about Horia.) -> washer_secret | washer_miss
* Good day. -> END

~ washer_want
Tereza: I came up from Vallaki for one autumn's picking, and that was four winters back.
Tereza [weary]: The moment the road's clear of twigs and teeth, I'm packing my kettle and walking home.
-> washer_menu

~ washer_secret
set tereza_sweet_known
Narrator: You notice that when she scolds Horia, she always makes sure his collar is turned down first.
Tereza: Well, someone has to keep an eye on the big ox, or he'd split his own boot with that axe.
Tereza [smile]: Vallaki's damp in the winter anyway. I suppose I can stay until he learns to mend a shirt.
-> washer_menu

~ washer_miss
Narrator: She wrings out a grey shirt as if it owes her coin and turns her back to the wind.
-> washer_menu

~ woodsplitter
Horia: I used to split staves for the casks. Now it's firewood. Same axe, same arms, worse smell. When we're home I'll make you a cask, if you like.
-> woodsplitter_menu

~ woodsplitter_menu
* Would you like your trade back? -> woodsplitter_want
* [if flag.tereza_sweet_known] Tereza is very cross with you. -> woodsplitter_secret
* Good day. -> END

~ woodsplitter_want
Horia: Good white oak wasn't grown to go up a chimney. It wants shaping and steaming and an iron hoop.
Horia [weary]: Give me one sound barrel to cooper before spring, so my hands remember they have a trade.
-> woodsplitter_menu

~ woodsplitter_secret
Narrator: A slow, dark red climbs from Horia's collar all the way to the tips of his ears.
Horia: She's got a sharp tongue on her, right enough. Sharpest in the hills.
Horia [smile]: She mended my mittens twice last week without my asking, though, so I let her shout.
-> woodsplitter_menu

~ pruner
Ovidiu: Dead, dead, dead, and this one's thinking about it. You cut away what won't come back, and you wait. That's all a vine-dresser is. Somebody good at waiting.
-> pruner_menu

~ pruner_menu
* What would you most like? -> pruner_want
* [if flag.ovidiu_want_heard] Which vines have you named? -> pruner_secret
* Good day. -> END

~ pruner_want
set ovidiu_want_heard
Ovidiu: Some folk talk to dogs. I talk to the old roots along the south wall, the ones I've given proper names.
Ovidiu [weary]: If every named vine puts out one green leaf before the frost takes us, I'll call that a good year.
-> pruner_menu

~ pruner_secret
Ovidiu [sad]: I gave each of the strong stocks a name for the Martikov children, so I'd remember to tend them twice.
Ovidiu: And the twisted one by the gate, I named that for young Elvir, who's gone to the dirt.
Ovidiu [sad]: All the others are holding on by their fingernails. Only Elvir's went dry in the night.
-> pruner_menu

~ picker
Andrei: These are the last good rows. Taste one. Sour, yes? The wine will be sweet. Don't ask me how. Ask the old man.
if not quest.the_black_row
quest the_black_row rumored
Andrei: Not the Seventh Row, though. Don't taste those. They come up black in the night and they're gone by morning, and I don't pick anything I didn't see grow.
elif quest.the_black_row == done
Andrei: The Seventh Row's young vines again. Sour as anything. I've never been so glad of sour.
endif
-> picker_menu

~ picker_menu
* (Watch him eat a grape.) -> picker_apology
* Good picking. -> END

~ picker_apology
Narrator: Andrei holds a bruised purple grape between thumb and forefinger, looking at it with real regret.
Andrei [sad]: Forgive me, little brother, you'd never have made a vintage anyway, and my mouth is very dry.
-> picker_menu

~ cooper
if flag.winery_wine_flows
Old Silviu [smile]: Hear that? That's a cask that holds. Davian's wine is going down the road again, in my casks. I could weep.
-> cooper_menu
endif
Old Silviu: Every hoop loose, every stave dry. The druids didn't touch the casks. They just let them die of neglect, which is worse.
-> cooper_menu

~ cooper_menu
* [if not quest.silvius_wedding_cask or quest.silvius_wedding_cask == asked or quest.silvius_wedding_cask == carrying] Is there anything we can carry for you? -> wizard_of_wines/silvius_cask:ask
* [if quest.silvius_wedding_cask == done] How did the wedding go? -> wizard_of_wines/silvius_cask:after
* Good day. -> END

~ raven
Narrator: The raven tilts its head and looks at you with one black eye, then the other, as if it is comparing notes. When you move, it hops after you, just far enough to keep watching.
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the raven what it's seen. -> raven_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the raven what it's seen.) -> raven_cast
* [if spell:speak_with_animals or knows:speak_with_animals] Let it keep watching. -> END
-> END

~ raven_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> raven_speaks
endif
-> END

# Speak with Animals (2024 PHB): the ravens are the Keepers of the Feather's eyes (Curse of Strahd, the Wizard of
# Wines): where the druids came from, where Davian hid his last stone, where the thief took the other.
~ raven_speaks
Narrator: The raven answers fast and low, like a scout making its report, and looks over its shoulder twice while it does.
if not flag.winery_reclaimed
set yester_hill_known
Narrator: "Green men sleep in the old man's house by day and walk the vines by night with the walking trees. They came from the hill to the west, where they're building a big man out of earth."
if not flag.winery_stone_hiding_told
set winery_stone_hiding_told
Narrator: "The old man's last green stone is in his cellar, in the oldest barrel at the foot of the stair. The third hoop turns too far. We watched him hide it. We watch everything."
endif
endif
if not quest.the_third_stone >= found
if not quest.the_third_stone
quest the_third_stone told
endif
Narrator: "The stone the thief took is in the drowned village down the river, in the old woman's hut that walks. We followed him there. We'll follow you, if you go."
endif
Narrator: "And the ring in our dead tree by the road falls slowly, like a feather. Take it. We have wings."
reveal roost_hoard
-> END
